  "problem_statement": "RIOT needs a portable way to obtain the system core clock frequency. Add a header `clk.h` that provides a function `uint32_t coreclk(void)` returning the current core clock frequency in Hz. Callers that need the core clock for delay loops or tick calculations must be able to include `clk.h` and call `coreclk()`. On native, a valid non-zero core clock value must be provided through this interface so existing callers build and run.",
